[
    {
        "content": "<p>I have a problem of building up a bimodule instance for ridiculously long time. </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">algebraHecke₁Op</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">bimoduleHecke₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- immediate</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">algebraHecke₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">bimoduleHecke₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- immediate</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">--30s to build up</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">--  |</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">--  ∨</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SMulCommClass</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">algebraHecke₁Op</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">algebraHecke₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">bimoduleHecke₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">constructor</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IntertwiningMap</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">comp_assoc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">unop'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- rather trivial proof</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Sorry I do not have an MWE and the above code is not complete. It eventually builds up while naive bimodule examples build up immediately and former instances also build up immediately. How to diagnose such things so that I could find an MWE?</p>",
        "id": 612104362,
        "sender_full_name": "Jiaxi Mo",
        "timestamp": 1784717456
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You can start with <code> set_option profiler true</code> to try to understand what is the culprit.</p>",
        "id": 612110814,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1784719791
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>it's a bit difficult without an example, but you will see what is taking so long (you may need to click various times, follow the biggest number).</p>",
        "id": 612110966,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1784719837
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Also, a good starting point is to understand if it is in the statement or in the proof.</p>",
        "id": 612111160,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1784719901
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I only saw one line <code>type checking took 26.4s</code> in the InfoView</p>",
        "id": 612112653,
        "sender_full_name": "Jiaxi Mo",
        "timestamp": 1784720400
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Sorry, copy/paste problem, use</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">trace</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Meta</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">synthInstance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">trace</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Meta</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isDefEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">trace</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">profiler</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 612120038,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1784722898
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Is everything fast if you replace the proof with <code>sorry</code>?</p>",
        "id": 612120164,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1784722939
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"130384\">Riccardo Brasca</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/bimodule.20instance.20diagnose/near/612120164\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Is everything fast if you replace the proof with <code>sorry</code>?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Thanks, now I see the one. </p>\n<p>[Elab.async] [28.437706] <span aria-label=\"check\" class=\"emoji emoji-2705\" role=\"img\" title=\"check\">:check:</span> _private.Lean.AddDecl.0.Lean.addDeclCore ▼</p>\n<p>[Kernel] [28.437643] <span aria-label=\"check\" class=\"emoji emoji-2705\" role=\"img\" title=\"check\">:check:</span> typechecking declarations [Representation.instSMulCommClassAlgebraHecke₁OpAlgebraHecke₁BimoduleHecke₁] </p>\n<p>It is fast if the proof is <code>sorry</code>. But the proof seems innocent to me where the lemma (not in Mathlib yet) is</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">comp_assoc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IntertwiningMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">τ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IntertwiningMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ρ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IntertwiningMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ρ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">comp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">comp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">comp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">comp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>and it can be replaced by <code>intro f g h; rfl</code> (but still 20-30s)</p>",
        "id": 612126344,
        "sender_full_name": "Jiaxi Mo",
        "timestamp": 1784724739
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I am on the phone so it's difficult to write code, but Lean is surely spending a lot of time in checking some defeq or not finding instances or a combination of the two. You have to dig into the trace, that is not super fun. You can look on zulip to see what people do to understand the trace.</p>",
        "id": 612132472,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1784726285
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>For example look at what is done <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Normed.20modules/near/511686343\">here</a>. If you have access to an LLM they're pretty good in reading those gigantic traces.</p>",
        "id": 612133310,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1784726537
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"130384\">Riccardo Brasca</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/bimodule.20instance.20diagnose/near/612133310\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>For example look at what is done <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Normed.20modules/near/511686343\">here</a>. If you have access to an LLM they're pretty good in reading those gigantic traces.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Indeed LLM is good at it and suggested a reasonable refactor. Although it is not totally clear to me what is happening, but the issue seems to be that there are too many layers around Hecke (opposites, intertwining, induction (coinvariant), trivial rep, subgroup embedding, End) and a solution is to move all primitive instances into Representation.IntertwiningMap where not Hecke structure is introduced. Probably I will make a seperate PR on that soon. Thanks a lot!</p>",
        "id": 612180676,
        "sender_full_name": "Jiaxi Mo",
        "timestamp": 1784738811
    }
]